      "message": "I am wondering if we can simplify the whole checking by moving all the check inside `NetlinkMessage` class like:\n```\npublic void assertNotErrorMessage() throws Exception {\n        if (mHeader \u003d\u003d null || mHeader.nlmsg_type \u003d\u003d NetlinkConstants.NLMSG_ERROR) {\n            throws new Exception(\"Asserion failed, ...\");\n        }\n}\n\npublic void assertNetlinkMessageType(short type) throws Exception {\n        if (mHeader \u003d\u003d null || hdr.nlmsg_type !\u003d type) {\n            throws new Exception(\"Asserion failed, ...\");\n        }\n}\n\n... \n```\nSo that we could do something like:\n\n```\n        try {\n            NetlinkMessage nlMsg \u003d extractNetlinkMessage(response);\n            nlMsg.ensureNotErrorMessage();\n            nlMsg.ensureNetlinkMessageType(NetlinkConstants.RTM_NEWLINK);\n            // other assertion\n        }\n```\nSo it looks cleaner and can possibly be reused in the future check.",
